1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,510
Section 2

2
00:00:01,510 --> 00:00:04,371
Welcome to this podcast about the Sheep market,

3
00:00:04,371 --> 00:00:07,090
which is one of the oldest parts of the city.

4
00:00:07,090 --> 00:00:11,484
As its name suggests, there was originally a market here where farmers brought their

5
00:00:11,484 --> 00:00:11,805
sheep,

6
00:00:11,805 --> 00:00:16,058
but now it's been redeveloped into a buzzing, vibrant area of the city,

7
00:00:16,058 --> 00:00:19,950
which is also home to one of the city's fastest-growing communities.

8
00:00:19,950 --> 00:00:23,977
The nearby university has always meant the area's popular with students,

9
00:00:23,977 --> 00:00:26,081
who come in to enjoy the lively nightlife,

10
00:00:26,081 --> 00:00:30,028
but now graduates embarking on careers in the worlds of fashion

11
00:00:30,028 --> 00:00:34,395
and design are buying up the new apartments recently built here to replace the

12
00:00:34,395 --> 00:00:37,160
small houses where the market workers used to live.

13
00:00:37,160 --> 00:00:42,179
The narrow old side streets are great places for finding original pictures, jewellery

14
00:00:42,179 --> 00:00:46,576
and ceramics which won't break the bank, as well as local produce like fruit

15
00:00:46,576 --> 00:00:47,720
and vegetables.

16
00:00:47,720 --> 00:00:51,102
There's also lots of pavement cafes where you can have a coffee

17
00:00:51,102 --> 00:00:53,820
and watch tourists from all over the world go by.

18
00:00:53,820 --> 00:00:57,999
The oldest buildings in the area are on the main streets, including the city's

19
00:00:57,999 --> 00:01:00,932
first department store, built in the 1880s,

20
00:01:00,932 --> 00:01:02,820
which is still open today.

21
00:01:02,820 --> 00:01:05,457
The Sheep market is a centre for fashion,

22
00:01:05,457 --> 00:01:08,980
and there's a policy of encouraging new young designers.

23
00:01:08,980 --> 00:01:13,534
The Young Fashion competition is open to local young people who are passionate about

24
00:01:13,534 --> 00:01:14,400
fashion.

25
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:18,417
This year they've been asked to design an outfit based on the ideas from the music

26
00:01:18,417 --> 00:01:24,020
and technology that's part of their everyday life, using both natural and man-made fibres.

27
00:01:24,020 --> 00:01:27,800
The garments will be judged by a panel of experts and fashion designers,

28
00:01:27,800 --> 00:01:31,480
and the winning entries will be modelled at a special gala evening.

29
00:01:31,480 --> 00:01:33,605
Parking at the Sheep market is easy.

30
00:01:33,605 --> 00:01:36,757
There are plenty of pay and display car parking spaces on the roadsides which

31
00:01:36,757 --> 00:01:40,024
are fine if you just want to stay for an hour or two,

32
00:01:40,024 --> 00:01:43,542
but if you want to spend the day there it's better to park in

33
00:01:43,542 --> 00:01:45,050
one of the for underground carparks.

34
00:01:45,050 --> 00:01:48,964
It's not expensive and if you can present a receipt from one of the

35
00:01:48,964 --> 00:01:51,200
local stores, you'll not be charged at all.

36
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:55,750
After six pm many of the car parks have a flat rate which varies

37
00:01:55,750 --> 00:01:57,700
but it is usually very reasonable.

38
00:01:57,700 --> 00:02:00,641
The Sheep market is one of the main centres for art

39
00:02:00,641 --> 00:02:02,780
and history in the whole of the country.

40
00:02:02,780 --> 00:02:06,840
If you look at our map, you'll see some of the main attractions there.

41
00:02:06,840 --> 00:02:10,320
Most visitors start from Crawley Road, at the bottom of the map.

42
00:02:10,320 --> 00:02:13,787
The Reynolds House is one of the oldest houses in the city,

43
00:02:13,787 --> 00:02:15,520
and is open to the public.

44
00:02:15,520 --> 00:02:20,521
It's on the north side of Crawley Road, next to the footpath that leads

45
00:02:20,521 --> 00:02:21,950
to the public gardens.

46
00:02:21,950 --> 00:02:24,983
The area's particularly interesting for its unusual sculptures.

47
00:02:24,983 --> 00:02:28,016
'The Thumb' is just what its name suggests,

48
00:02:28,016 --> 00:02:30,291
but it's about 10 metres high.

49
00:02:30,291 --> 00:02:34,840
You'll see it on Hill Road, across the road from the Bank.

50
00:02:34,840 --> 00:02:39,400
The Museum's got a particularly fine collection of New Zealand landscapes.

51
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:43,523
It's on the east side of the Sheep market, on City Road.

52
00:02:43,523 --> 00:02:48,332
It's on the other side of the road from the public gardens, immediately facing

53
00:02:48,332 --> 00:02:50,050
the junction with Hill Road.

54
00:02:50,050 --> 00:02:54,565
The Contemporary Art Gallery is on a little road that leads off Station Square,

55
00:02:54,565 --> 00:02:56,500
not far from the public gardens.

56
00:02:56,500 --> 00:03:02,042
The road ends at the gallery - it doesn't go anywhere else.That's open every

57
00:03:02,042 --> 00:03:03,230
day except Mondays.

58
00:03:03,230 --> 00:03:06,022
The Warner Gallery specialises in 19th-century art.

59
00:03:06,022 --> 00:03:11,608
It's on City Road, near the junction with Crawley Road, on the same side

60
00:03:11,608 --> 00:03:14,400
of the road as the public gardens.

61
00:03:14,400 --> 00:03:17,920
It's open on weekdays from 9 to 5,

62
00:03:17,920 --> 00:03:19,680
and entry is free.

63
00:03:19,680 --> 00:03:25,840
Finally, if you're interested in purchasing high quality artwork, the place to go is

64
00:03:25,840 --> 00:03:26,280
Nucleus.

65
00:03:26,280 --> 00:03:29,990
You need to go from Crawley Road up through Station Square

66
00:03:29,990 --> 00:03:34,713
and east along Hill Road until you get to a small winding road turning

67
00:03:34,713 --> 00:03:35,050
off.

68
00:03:35,050 --> 00:03:39,867
Go up there and it's on your right - if you get to City

69
00:03:39,867 --> 00:03:41,720
Road you've gone too far.
